        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(web): unify desktop shell chrome into one Slack-style surface",
        "body": "Second pass on the shell chrome (follows #61): instead of stacked bars with borders, the desktop app now uses Slack's unified-surface model.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **One continuous chrome surface.** The title bar, workspace rail, and sidebar share a single dotted plate (the Switchboard mounting-plate texture); their individual backgrounds and dividing borders are gone. The conversation floats on the plate as a rounded card with a hairline border — top corners square off when the thread/profile or artifact pane joins the card.\n- **Sidebar workspace header removed on desktop.** The workspace name moved into the title bar's dead space next to the sidebar toggle; clicking it opens workspace settings. The chevron menu button is gone. The sidebar gains the full 60px row back for channels, and its grid drops to list + user card.\n- **Connection state follows the name.** The pulsing \"Connecting…\" note renders beside the workspace name in the title bar, only while the realtime link is down.\n- Narrow windows (≤820px) restore opaque surfaces for the rail/sidebar since they become overlay drawers there. The browser app keeps the sidebar workspace header unchanged.\n- E2E: desktop test now asserts no sidebar header, and clicks the title-bar workspace button through to the workspace-settings dialog; the native-frame test asserts the header remains on web.\n\n## Proof\n\nLight: ![unified chrome light](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openclaw/clickclack/claude/unified-shell-chrome/docs/proof/shell-chrome-unified-light.png)\n\nDark: ![unified chrome dark](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openclaw/clickclack/claude/unified-shell-chrome/docs/proof/shell-chrome-unified-dark.png)\n\n- Rebased onto #62 (agent-activity pinning); changelog conflict resolved, embedded assets rebuilt from the merged tree.\n- `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm fmt:ts:check`, `pnpm build` green; targeted e2e 7/7 (desktop titlebar, Windows caption space, native-frame fallback, connection state, boot, collapse, agent activity).\n- Autoreview (Codex gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh): clean, no actionable findings.\n",
